note forbnd benchmark control mb-ctl (body after a lead line): mb-sum with the count in a variable, so the
note rule does not apply; om2 and om2 bce give byte-identical programs and the A/B difference is noise.
global a ulong 4096
fn main to int
for i ulong 4096
put a i mul i 7
end
n = ulong 4096
s = ulong 0
for r ulong 20000
for i ulong n
s = add s get a i
end
end
ret int rem s 251
end
